    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Neonates w severe cyanosis: PGE1 infusion (start 0.05–0.1 mcg/kg/min IV) opens the ductus arteriosus and ↑pulmonary blood flow."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Hypercyanotic spell that persists after positioning, O2 and IV fluids: morphine, phenylephrine and BBs (propranolol or esmolol). Propranolol 0.25–1 mg/kg PO q6h until surgical repair may prevent recurrences."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Endocarditis prophylaxis: preop, then only for the first 6 mo after repair unless a residual defect sits next to a surgical patch or prosthetic material."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
